To establish a rich and comprehensive annotation set for chest X-rays, we created
CAXR-CT, a resource that includes detailed markings on chest X-ray images based
on their corresponding CT scans. Our annotation set, consisting of 200 distinct
markers, spans from normal lung function to various severe pathologies. Following
a traditional competition-style process, a 5-minute task was assigned to 57 medical
specialists, resulting in 13 findings. Leading the CAXR-CT challenge, team 'DeepBreaht'
consisted of three members, consisting of two computer scientists and a medical
specialist, who using a designed pipeline that integrated vision and language
capabilities, achieved top scores across all competition stages. In this paper, we
will detail our annotation set, followed by the winning approach employed by team
'DeepBreaht. 

